{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1483465-tell-me-your-core-mortal-stories","id":1483465,"title":"Tell me your core mortal stories","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-09T08:14:35-07:00","id":1483465,"title":"Tell me your core mortal stories","content":"What sais in the title, i\u00b4d like to know about interesting campaigns you have played in or run using the core mortal rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27340-anyoneatall","name":"Anyoneatall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T01:05:23-07:00","id":1483701,"title":"","content":"Is this that noone is interested in telling them or that noone has any core mortal story?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27340-anyoneatall","name":"Anyoneatall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T03:32:36-07:00","id":1483711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anyoneatall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1483465-tell-me-your-core-mortal-stories#post1483465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What sais in the title, i\u00b4d like to know about interesting campaigns you have played in or run using the core mortal rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I once runned a short 3 session prelude, not a campaing.<br /> I think that with so much material about monsters few peoples are willing to go an entire chronicle with a simple human pc, but it s only my opinion.<br /> Anyway, i setted it in the Dark eras scenario about the Black plague in Italy.<br /> Pc where all villagers in a small rural village near Florence.<br /> Only 2 of them had supernatural merits, a nun with Medium and the daughter of a charcoal burner with Psichometry.<br /> During the night before Christmas, the local priest went missing, returning the morning after with a large wound on the head.<br /> After that, womens in the village started being murdered in strange or misterious ways.<br /> The pc where all close friends of the priest, and started investigating those events.<br /> In short, womens of the ruling families of the village were all born with Psichometry, a gift that allowed them to discover the key of an Avernian gateway in a nearby roman s temple ruins.<br /> Over the course of a century a cult has been formed around an artifact found in the temple, wich the gifted women coul learn to use to summon a powerful ghost from the open gate.<br /> Once a year, they would kidnap a lonely traveler or pilgrim, celebrate a ritual orgy/feast in the temple, and then offer the traveler and a cup of fine wine to the ghost, in exchange for a bag full of silver.<br /> But in that year the priest started investigating the missings, and ended witnessing the ritual.<br /> The artifact used was Supernal in nature, and the Sleepee witness botched the ritual, summoning instead a murderous ghost who fettered on the priest.<br /> The priest escaped in terror, with nobody seeing him, but running wildly he tripped on the ruined temple floor, hurting his head and leaving bloodstains (a clue).<br /> The ghost started to gradually increase the manifestation condition on the priest, with the final aim to claim him.<br /> The city elders doesn t know this, but started hindering the investigations of the pc fearing the exposure of their secret ritual.<br /> The scenario ended with the discovery and crafting of the ghost s bane, followed by the exorcism of the half claimed priest escaped in the forest.<br /> <br /> The players liked it, a good introduction to the various game mechanics","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T15:59:54-07:00","id":1483759,"title":"","content":"I actually rather enjoy running or playing &quot;Mortal&quot; games.<br /> <br /> Last year I ran two The first was a stand alone story about a group of college friends staying at a ski resort in the Swiss alps. it had a survival horror feel. The town around the resort was a cult that worshiped &quot;the God under the Mountain&quot; and sought to turn one of the friends into a wendigo. there was the previous wendigo, The ski resort had a history of mysterious deaths and was full of ghost and at the center of the cult there was a witch. it was all very good fun, if i recall correctly only two of the ten of the potential player characters survived, and one was captured with the final scene of them having to chose between eating a human heart or starve.<br /> <br /> I did a few things that were a bit strange for a World of Darkness game, firstly all the characters in the friend group I pre-made. There were twice as many potential player character as players and i let the players choose based on a list of names and short descriptions. this allowed any character death to not be a big deal and allow the player to pick up a new character sheet and continue. One of the characters had prophetic dreams.<br /> There was a traitor in the group that led them there, I'm not sure of it was fortunate or unfortunate but no player picked the traitor as their character but without a doubt the reveal was my favorite part.<br /> The whole thing took about five or six sessions but I'm a little long winded.<br /> <br /> <br /> The second &quot;Mortal&quot; game i ran was call Carrion City Chronicles, sadly we didn't finish the main story before life got in the way and it got put on permanent hiatus. but it was a campaign/sandbox style murder mystery, with lots of politics and strange occult happenings. It had a Twin Peaks vibe and was pretty amazing. A rouge priest was being urged (not quite a full possession but more a manipulated spirit anchor) by an angel and immolating the people he touched, after his first few accidents he came to the conclusion that he was gifted this power to smite the wicked and began to immolate people he viewed as evil. One of the players was a member of the Malleus Maleficarum, The Knight's of Saint George once used the cities cathedral as a base it latter became the players base of operations as well. The game was full of crooked cops, bikers, a hit-man for the God Machine, ghosts, gun fights, and oh so many charred corpses. I really loved it.<br /> again it probably had half dozen sessions or so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}